      "focus": "Engage Colleague 8 directly. Graciously concede that lines 27–28 are in Canto 1, not Canto 2. Then build on Colleague 8's exact note regarding early childhood orphanhood: show that an intrusive boyhood memory of detective fiction immediately following the sudden death of parents is the archetypal embodiment of 'the surprise of interrupted grief' (Option 4). Contrast this psychological specificity with the generic nature of 'persistence after death'.",
      "textual_wedge_on_A": "Press the logical paradox on Doyle's text: Holmes explicitly states he did NOT reverse his boots. Shade asks about someone who DID reverse his shoes. Therefore, attributing it to Holmes contradicts both Doyle and Shade's syntax ('that fellow in Sherlock Holmes'). Moran remains the only operational figure."
    }
  },
