      "Option_4_Empty_House_Holmes": "Decisively supported by Conan Doyle's text in 'The Adventure of the Empty House'. Holmes explicitly discusses 'my boots' ('I might, it is true, have reversed my boots...'). The prompt's subjunctive phrasing ('to whom would the reversed shoes have properly belonged?') directly reflects that the maneuver was contemplated hypothetically by Holmes for his own footwear. Moran was perched overhead firing an air-gun and rolling rocks; he never wore, discussed, or contemplated reversed footwear. The claim that the shoes belonged to Moran is an outright factual error.",
